  "interpretation": [
    "Equivalent physical cutoffs 0.5 nm, 5 angstrom and 500 pm change the exact-boundary outcome under different active length policies. Raw conversions to nm already show one-to-two float64 steps below 0.5 for the latter inputs.",
    "Both native dense and cell-list routes reproduce the discrepancy; ordinary and trusted native calls agree in every recorded case. A blanket approximate comparison is not an accepted scientific correction.",
    "The immediate float64 predecessor of 0.5 nm remains a negative control. Preserve original caller unit/value and inspect both threshold digestion and calculation/presentation unit choices.",
    "The provider review asks for an existing supported API or a bounded general conversion/comparison contract. It does not assert that ordinary IEEE backend rounding violates an existing PyUnitWizard promise.",
    "The prototype tests deliberately use a tiny configured numeric-output budget. Their MemoryPressureWarnings refer to that test budget; monitored host pressure and cgroup stops are recorded independently.",
    "No sibling checkout, package, native backend, unit policy or environment is changed. The published 0.28.1 payload remains the runtime provider; the clean inspected f82b618 source is not substituted."
  ],
